{"bank":"mathleague","grades":[8],"papers":[["mathleague/2004-05-g8",{"contest":"Math League","paper":"2004-05 Grade 8 Contest","year":2005,"url":"https://www.mathleague.com/index.php/annualcontestinformation/samplecontests"}],["mathleague/2012-13-g8",{"contest":"Math League","paper":"2012-13 Grade 8 Contest","year":2013,"url":"https://www.mathleague.com/index.php/annualcontestinformation/samplecontests"}],["mathleague/2018-19-g8",{"contest":"Math League","paper":"2018-19 Grade 8 Contest","year":2019,"url":"https://www.mathleague.com/index.php/annualcontestinformation/samplecontests"}]],"questions":[{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-01","type":"mc","prompt":"$1110-1020=110-\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"102"},{"key":"B","text":"101"},{"key":"C","text":"90"},{"key":"D","text":"20"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":1},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-02","type":"mc","prompt":"If my doctor's \"IN\" sign is a square with a perimeter of 4, then its area is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"16"}],"answer":"A","topics":["geometry"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":2},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-03","type":"mc","prompt":"$300\\div200=1\\div\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac13$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac12$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac23$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac32$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":3},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-04","type":"mc","prompt":"When written as an improper fraction, five-fourths is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac45$"},{"key":"B","text":"$1\\frac14$"},{"key":"C","text":"1.25"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac54$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":4},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-05","type":"mc","prompt":"$2005-2005-2004=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"-2004"},{"key":"C","text":"-2005"},{"key":"D","text":"-2006"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":5},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-06","type":"mc","prompt":"Exactly 120 seconds after midnight, the correct time is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12:02 P.M."},{"key":"B","text":"12:02 A.M."},{"key":"C","text":"2 P.M."},{"key":"D","text":"2 A.M."}],"answer":"B","topics":["time-calendar"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":6},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-07","type":"mc","prompt":"$24\\div4\\times2+4=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"7"},{"key":"C","text":"16"},{"key":"D","text":"36"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":7},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-08","type":"mc","prompt":"The reciprocal of $\\left(\\frac12\\times4\\right)$ is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$2\\times\\frac14$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac12\\times4$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac12\\times\\frac14$"},{"key":"D","text":"$2\\times4$"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":8},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-09","type":"mc","prompt":"Of the following numbers, which is closest in value to 1?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.995"},{"key":"B","text":"0.99"},{"key":"C","text":"1.01"},{"key":"D","text":"1.1"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":9},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-10","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the sum of all the one-digit positive prime numbers?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"15"},{"key":"B","text":"16"},{"key":"C","text":"17"},{"key":"D","text":"18"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":10},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-11","type":"mc","prompt":"$2\\times\\frac12\\times4\\times\\frac14\\times6\\times\\frac16=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"24"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":11},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-12","type":"mc","prompt":"When I add the measures of *any* 2 angles of triangle $T$, the sum is always $120^\\circ$. Triangle $T$ *must* be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"scalene"},{"key":"B","text":"right"},{"key":"C","text":"obtuse"},{"key":"D","text":"equiangular"}],"answer":"D","topics":["geometry","logic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":12},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-13","type":"mc","prompt":"I wear my headphones only on cloudy days. The day after each cloudy day is a sunny day. I wear my headphones at most \\underline{\\;?\\;} times in a week.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"5"},{"key":"D","text":"6"}],"answer":"B","topics":["logic","counting"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":13},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-14","type":"mc","prompt":"Of the following, which has the largest value?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"7"},{"key":"B","text":"$(-1)^2$"},{"key":"C","text":"$(-2)^2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$(-3)^2$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":14},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-15","type":"mc","prompt":"$9000\\%+900\\%+90\\%+9\\%=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"9999"},{"key":"B","text":"999.9"},{"key":"C","text":"99.99"},{"key":"D","text":"0.9999"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":15},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-16","type":"mc","prompt":"A dealer paid Bunny Fabergé 50 pennies for each of his decorated eggs. The dealer then sold each egg for 50 quarters. Bunny (the artist) got what percent of the final purchase price?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2%"},{"key":"B","text":"4%"},{"key":"C","text":"25%"},{"key":"D","text":"50%"}],"answer":"B","topics":["fractions-decimals","money"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":16},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-17","type":"mc","prompt":"$\\sqrt{\\sqrt{\\sqrt{256}}}=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"16"}],"answer":"A","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":17},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-18","type":"mc","prompt":"$30\\%\\times40\\%=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12%"},{"key":"B","text":"120%"},{"key":"C","text":"1200%"},{"key":"D","text":"12 000%"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":18},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-19","type":"mc","prompt":"The number \\underline{\\;?\\;} has exactly 4 different whole number factors.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"30"},{"key":"B","text":"24"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"10"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":19},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-20","type":"mc","prompt":"When rounded to the nearest *fifth*, 0.33 becomes","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.2"},{"key":"B","text":"0.3"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac25$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac35$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":20},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-21","type":"mc","prompt":"I lost my coins! This morning, I had 7 coins worth 49¢. How many nickels did I have?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"1"},{"key":"C","text":"2"},{"key":"D","text":"7"}],"answer":"A","topics":["money","logic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":21},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-22","type":"mc","prompt":"$1.5\\text{ m}+60\\text{ cm}+0.02\\text{ km}=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.221 m"},{"key":"B","text":"2.21 m"},{"key":"C","text":"22.1 m"},{"key":"D","text":"221 m"}],"answer":"C","topics":["measurement"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":22},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-23","type":"mc","prompt":"How many of the positive multiples of 2 are factors of 222?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"111"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"3"},{"key":"D","text":"1"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":23},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-24","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the average of the first 99 positive whole numbers?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"49.00"},{"key":"B","text":"49.50"},{"key":"C","text":"49.75"},{"key":"D","text":"50.00"}],"answer":"D","topics":["statistics","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":24},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-25","type":"mc","prompt":"If a small circle's diameter is a large circle's radius, then the small circle's area is \\underline{\\;?\\;}% of the large circle's area.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"20"},{"key":"B","text":"25"},{"key":"C","text":"40"},{"key":"D","text":"50"}],"answer":"B","topics":["geometry","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":25},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-26","type":"mc","prompt":"If $\\frac23$ of a cup of fish food can feed 8 goldfish, then 4 cups of fish food should be able to feed \\underline{\\;?\\;} goldfish.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"24"},{"key":"C","text":"36"},{"key":"D","text":"48"}],"answer":"D","topics":["rates","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":26},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-27","type":"mc","prompt":"An integer *cannot* be \\underline{\\;?\\;} if its square is even.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"prime"},{"key":"B","text":"odd"},{"key":"C","text":"even"},{"key":"D","text":"zero"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory","logic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":27},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-28","type":"mc","prompt":"If $4x=$ the reciprocal of $\\frac{1}{x^3}$, then $x$ could equal","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac18$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac12$"},{"key":"C","text":"2"},{"key":"D","text":"8"}],"answer":"C","topics":["algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":28},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-29","type":"mc","prompt":"$2^{10}\\times2^{10}=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$2^{20}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2^{100}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$4^{20}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4^{100}$"}],"answer":"A","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":29},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-30","type":"mc","prompt":"I got immunized on the one millionth second of this calendar year. That happened on","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"January 11"},{"key":"B","text":"January 12"},{"key":"C","text":"February 1"},{"key":"D","text":"February 2"}],"answer":"B","topics":["time-calendar","measurement"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":30},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-31","type":"mc","prompt":"$\\sqrt{16^{16}}=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$4^4$"},{"key":"B","text":"$4^8$"},{"key":"C","text":"$16^4$"},{"key":"D","text":"$16^8$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":31},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-32","type":"mc","prompt":"Each of 2005 fractions has an even numerator and an odd denominator. If the product of all of them is an integer, it must be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"even"},{"key":"B","text":"odd"},{"key":"C","text":"prime"},{"key":"D","text":"2005"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory","logic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":32},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-33","type":"mc","prompt":"If $x$ is a whole number, what is the largest possible perimeter of a triangle with side-lengths 3, 4, and $x$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"11"},{"key":"B","text":"12"},{"key":"C","text":"13"},{"key":"D","text":"14"}],"answer":"C","topics":["geometry"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":33},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-34","type":"mc","prompt":"When fully expanded, $10\\,000^{9999}$ has \\underline{\\;?\\;} digits.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"9999"},{"key":"B","text":"10 000"},{"key":"C","text":"39 996"},{"key":"D","text":"39 997"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory","arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":34},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-35","type":"mc","prompt":"In the diagram, the total number of different triangles is","image":"qimages/mathleague/2004-05-g8/q35.webp","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"3"},{"key":"C","text":"4"},{"key":"D","text":"5"}],"answer":"C","topics":["geometry","counting","spatial"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":35},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-36","type":"mc","prompt":"If the sum of 2000 consecutive integers is 1000, then the sum of the digits of the *greatest* of these 2000 integers is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"9"},{"key":"D","text":"27"}],"answer":"A","topics":["algebra","sequences-series"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":36},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-37","type":"mc","prompt":"How many of the 15 positive factors of 400 are divisible by 4?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"8"},{"key":"C","text":"9"},{"key":"D","text":"10"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory","counting"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":37},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-38","type":"mc","prompt":"I phoned my mom to help me answer this, the final question on a quiz show: *How many integers equal their own squares?* Mom said, \"?\" She was right!","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"zero"},{"key":"B","text":"one"},{"key":"C","text":"two"},{"key":"D","text":"three"}],"answer":"C","topics":["algebra","number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":38},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-39","type":"mc","prompt":"At 12:22, a clock's hour hand is \\underline{\\;?\\;} away from a vertical position.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$10^\\circ$"},{"key":"B","text":"$11^\\circ$"},{"key":"C","text":"$21^\\circ$"},{"key":"D","text":"$22^\\circ$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["time-calendar","geometry"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":39},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g8-40","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the tens' digit of the product $1\\times2\\times3\\times\\ldots\\times98\\times99$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"0"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":40},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-01","type":"mc","prompt":"$(1 + 4 + 1 + 4)\\times\\underline{\\;?\\;} = 14\\,140$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"1010"},{"key":"C","text":"1414"},{"key":"D","text":"10 000"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":1},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-02","type":"mc","prompt":"The number of fish in a giant sandwich is divisible by 2, 3, 4, and 5. There could be $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ fish.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2345"},{"key":"B","text":"4567"},{"key":"C","text":"5550"},{"key":"D","text":"6660"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":2},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-03","type":"mc","prompt":"The average of 25 and $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ is 2013.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"994"},{"key":"B","text":"1019"},{"key":"C","text":"1988"},{"key":"D","text":"4001"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic","statistics"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":3},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-04","type":"mc","prompt":"Bob rides his bicycle at 40 km per hour. How far will Bob ride in 3 minutes?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1 km"},{"key":"B","text":"2 km"},{"key":"C","text":"3 km"},{"key":"D","text":"4 km"}],"answer":"B","topics":["rates"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":4},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-05","type":"mc","prompt":"I am waiting in line with 10 people in front of me, including my brother. My brother has 10 people behind him in line, including me. If my brother is right in front of me, how many people are in line?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"11"},{"key":"B","text":"19"},{"key":"C","text":"20"},{"key":"D","text":"21"}],"answer":"C","topics":["logic","counting"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":5},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-06","type":"mc","prompt":"Each of my 60 books has either a hard cover or a soft cover. If I have 4 times as many hard covers as soft covers, I have $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ hard covers.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"48"},{"key":"B","text":"35"},{"key":"C","text":"15"},{"key":"D","text":"12"}],"answer":"A","topics":["algebra","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":6},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-07","type":"mc","prompt":"The largest odd factor of 111 is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"37"},{"key":"C","text":"109"},{"key":"D","text":"111"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":7},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-08","type":"mc","prompt":"My coin jar has 100 pennies, 200 nickels, 300 dimes, and 400 quarters in it. The coins have a total value of","choices":[{"key":"A","text