 of diamonds Axel found was the least common multiple of 18, 28, and 38, he found $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ diamonds.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"84"},{"key":"C","text":"4788"},{"key":"D","text":"19 152"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":14},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-15","type":"mc","prompt":"7 hundredths + 7 thousandths = 7 tenths − $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.623"},{"key":"B","text":"0.777"},{"key":"C","text":"0.784"},{"key":"D","text":"0.854"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":15},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-16","type":"mc","prompt":"$2^2\\times2^2\\times2^2 + 2^2\\times2^2 + 2^2 = 2^2\\times\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"16"},{"key":"B","text":"21"},{"key":"C","text":"32"},{"key":"D","text":"33"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":16},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-17","type":"mc","prompt":"If I multiply the number of math contests I have taken in my life by 6 and then add 5, the resulting number *cannot* be divisible by","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"7"},{"key":"C","text":"9"},{"key":"D","text":"11"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":17},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-18","type":"mc","prompt":"An evil witch casts a spell to put a princess to sleep for 10 000 hours. If the princess falls asleep at 6:00 P.M., she will wake at","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10:00 A.M."},{"key":"B","text":"4:00 P.M."},{"key":"C","text":"8:00 P.M."},{"key":"D","text":"11:00 P.M."}],"answer":"A","topics":["time-calendar"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":18},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-19","type":"mc","prompt":"Of the rocks in a box, 1/3 are igneous, 60 are metamorphic, and the remaining 40% are sedimentary. How many rocks are in the box?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"160"},{"key":"B","text":"180"},{"key":"C","text":"200"},{"key":"D","text":"225"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals","algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":19},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-20","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of 4 consecutive even integers is 148. The sum of the digits of the smallest of the 4 integers is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"7"},{"key":"C","text":"9"},{"key":"D","text":"12"}],"answer":"B","topics":["algebra","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":20},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-21","type":"mc","prompt":"Max has 9 pairs of glasses for every 2 surfboards he has. If he has 108 pairs of glasses, he has $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ surfboards.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"24"},{"key":"C","text":"48"},{"key":"D","text":"486"}],"answer":"B","topics":["rates","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":21},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-22","type":"mc","prompt":"$180 + 150\\%$ of $180 =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"270"},{"key":"B","text":"330"},{"key":"C","text":"450"},{"key":"D","text":"630"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":22},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-23","type":"mc","prompt":"The perimeter of a triangle is 50. The length of the longest side of the triangle could be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"15"},{"key":"B","text":"20"},{"key":"C","text":"25"},{"key":"D","text":"29"}],"answer":"B","topics":["geometry","inequalities"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":23},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-24","type":"mc","prompt":"If $x \\,\\square\\, y$ is defined as $(x + y)^2 - 2xy$, then $5 \\,\\square\\, 7 =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"24"},{"key":"C","text":"35"},{"key":"D","text":"74"}],"answer":"D","topics":["algebra"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":24},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-25","type":"mc","prompt":"A square of side-length $4\\pi$ has the same perimeter as a circle of diameter","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"16"}],"answer":"D","topics":["geometry","measurement"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":25},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-26","type":"mc","prompt":"Sprinkles the dog likes to chase marching bands. When he does, he runs at 18 km per hour, which is the same as running at $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ m per second.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"10"},{"key":"D","text":"18"}],"answer":"A","topics":["rates","measurement"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":26},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-27","type":"mc","prompt":"If the sum of 2 integers is 25, the product of the integers could *not* be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"-150"},{"key":"B","text":"-30"},{"key":"C","text":"100"},{"key":"D","text":"154"}],"answer":"B","topics":["algebra","number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":27},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-28","type":"mc","prompt":"How many of the first 1000 positive integers are multiples of both 4 and 5 but not of 6?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"34"},{"key":"B","text":"42"},{"key":"C","text":"50"},{"key":"D","text":"58"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory","counting"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":28},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-29","type":"mc","prompt":"$\\frac35 : 6 = 8 : \\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{20}{9}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac95$"},{"key":"C","text":"24"},{"key":"D","text":"80"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals","algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":29},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-30","type":"mc","prompt":"If the average of three positive integers is 5, the greatest possible value of the sum of the squares of the three integers is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"107"},{"key":"B","text":"149"},{"key":"C","text":"171"},{"key":"D","text":"197"}],"answer":"C","topics":["algebra","inequalities"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":30},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-31","type":"mc","prompt":"After a long walk yesterday, Cody wants to go 50% farther today in half as much time. What percent faster will she have to walk today than she did yesterday to meet her goal?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"200%"},{"key":"B","text":"300%"},{"key":"C","text":"400%"},{"key":"D","text":"500%"}],"answer":"A","topics":["rates","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":31},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-32","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the greatest prime factor of $9^{18} - 3^{32}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"17"},{"key":"C","text":"19"},{"key":"D","text":"31"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":32},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-33","type":"mc","prompt":"How many factors of $3\\times6\\times9\\times12\\times15\\times18$ are greater than 1 and are the square of an integer?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"15"},{"key":"B","text":"14"},{"key":"C","text":"7"},{"key":"D","text":"6"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory","counting"],"difficulty":3,"p":1,"n":33},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-34","type":"mc","prompt":"Each time Bette fills out a form, she marks *just one* box: A, B, or C. If she checks boxes at random, the probability that in filling out 3 such forms she will mark one each of A, B, and C is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac14$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac13$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac29$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{3}{10}$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["probability"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":34},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g8-35","type":"mc","prompt":"In the sequence 105, 107, 112, 114, …, every number besides 105 and 107 is 7 greater than an earlier number. Which of the following may appear in this sequence?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1296"},{"key":"B","text":"1648"},{"key":"C","text":"2137"},{"key":"D","text":"2818"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory","sequences-series"],"difficulty":3,"p":1,"n":35},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-01","type":"mc","prompt":"$(4 \\times 6 \\times 8 \\times 10) \\div (6 \\times 8 \\times 10) =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"$3\\times6\\times8\\times10$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":1},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-02","type":"mc","prompt":"$(2 \\div 3)$ rounded to the nearest hundredth is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.33"},{"key":"B","text":"0.66"},{"key":"C","text":"0.67"},{"key":"D","text":"0.70"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":2},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-03","type":"mc","prompt":"Baby Amy is one day older than Baby Barry. The product of their ages measured in days could be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"33"},{"key":"B","text":"132"},{"key":"C","text":"245"},{"key":"D","text":"246"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":3},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-04","type":"mc","prompt":"(The largest even divisor of 200) $\\div$ (the largest odd divisor of 200) $=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"8"},{"key":"C","text":"20"},{"key":"D","text":"200"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":4},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-05","type":"mc","prompt":"An equilateral triangle with integer side-lengths has a perimeter that is numerically equal to the area of a square. Which of the following could be the length of a side of the square?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"10"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"4"}],"answer":"A","topics":["geometry","number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":5},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-06","type":"mc","prompt":"I have only nickels, dimes, and quarters to pay for my dinner, which costs \\$12.60. The smallest number of coins I can use to pay is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"51"},{"key":"B","text":"52"},{"key":"C","text":"54"},{"key":"D","text":"55"}],"answer":"A","topics":["money"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":6},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-07","type":"mc","prompt":"The smallest prime factor of 2019 is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"3"},{"key":"C","text":"19"},{"key":"D","text":"673"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":7},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-08","type":"mc","prompt":"The product of four consecutive integers must be divisible by each of the following *except*","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"10"},{"key":"D","text":"12"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":8},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-09","type":"mc","prompt":"There are $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ hours in 4 weeks.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"48"},{"key":"B","text":"96"},{"key":"C","text":"336"},{"key":"D","text":"672"}],"answer":"D","topics":["time-calendar"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":9},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-10","type":"mc","prompt":"If I divide my favorite number by its reciprocal, the quotient is 10 times as large as my favorite number. My favorite number is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac1{10}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac15$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac12$"},{"key":"D","text":"10"}],"answer":"D","topics":["algebra","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":10},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-11","type":"mc","prompt":"The height of the smoke from my barbecue is 100 000 cm, which is the same as $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ km.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"10"},{"key":"C","text":"100"},{"key":"D","text":"1000"}],"answer":"A","topics":["measurement"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":11},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-12","type":"mc","prompt":"If the degree measures of the angles of a triangle are in a 4:5:6 ratio, what is the difference between the measures of the largest and the smallest angles?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$12^\\circ$"},{"key":"B","text":"$24^\\circ$"},{"key":"C","text":"$30^\\circ$"},{"key":"D","text":"$36^\\circ$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["geometry"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":12},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-13","type":"mc","prompt":"The population of a town started at 1000, then went up 10%, then down 20%, then back up 10%. The population of the town ended at","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"968"},{"key":"B","text":"972"},{"key":"C","text":"1000"},{"key":"D","text":"1024"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":13},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-14","type":"mc","prompt":"In my orchard, there are 60 more apples than oranges, and 5 times as many apples as oranges. How many apples are there?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"50"},{"key":"B","text":"75"},{"key":"C","text":"100"},{"key":"D","text":"125"}],"answer":"B","topics":["algebra"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":14},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-15","type":"mc","prompt":"A polygon in which every pair of angles is supplementary *must* be a","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"triangle"},{"key":"B","text":"square"},{"key":"C","text":"rectangle"},{"key":"D","text":"hexagon"}],"answer":"C","topics":["geometry"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":15},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-16","type":"mc","prompt":"Which of the following is smallest in value?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$2^{600}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$3^{500}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$4^{400}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$5^{300}$"}],"answer":"A","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":16},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-17","type":"mc","prompt":"$(2^{100} \\times 4^{50}) \\div 2 =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$2^{75}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2^{100}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2^{149}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$2^{199}$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":17},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-18","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the remainder when $3^{333}$ is divided by 10?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"3"},{"key":"C","text":"7"},{"key":"D","text":"9"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory","patterns"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":18},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-19","type":"mc","prompt":"On a series of tests, Gus got 100 once, 90 twice, and 80 five times. What was his average score for all of the tests?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"80"},{"key":"B","text":"85"},{"key":"C","text":"90"},{"key":"D","text":"92"}],"answer":"B","topics":["statistics"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":19},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-20","type":"mc","prompt":"The product of the **thousands** and **tenths** digits of 1234.5678 is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"10"},{"key":"C","text":"35"},{"key":"D","text":"40"}],"answer":"A","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":20},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-21","type":"mc","prompt":"The probability of heads then tails then heads on 3 tosses of a coin is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.125"},{"key":"B","text":"0.25"},{"key":"C","text":"0.375"},{"key":"D","text":"0.5"}],"answer":"A","topics":["probability"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":21},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-22","type":"mc","prompt":"On January 1 last year, Rui got a jar of jellybeans. On each day he ate the same number of jellybeans. He counted 560 on January 31 before eating any and he counted 380 on March 17 before eating any. There were $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ jellybeans in the jar when Rui got it.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"600"},{"key":"B","text":"650"},{"key":"C","text":"680"},{"key":"D","text":"740"}],"answer":"C","topics":["rates","time-calendar"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":22},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-23","type":"mc","prompt":"Jake used 120 boxes of tissues in 3 days! There are 144 tissues per box. That's $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ tissues per minute!","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"3"},{"key":"C","text":"4"},{"key":"D","text":"5"}],"answer":"C","topics":["rates"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":23},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-24","type":"mc","prompt":"The number 5184 has $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ positive odd divisors.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"4"},{"key":"D","text":"5"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":24},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-25","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of 5 consecutive even integers could be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"120"},{"key":"B","text":"125"},{"key":"C","text":"164"},{"key":"D","text":"212"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":25},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-26","type":"mc","prompt":"Jacques, who paints only smiley faces, signs and numbers each of his paintings. If he started with Smiley #1 and has painted through Smiley #111, how many times has he used the digit 1 in his numbering?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"22"},{"key":"C","text":"24"},{"key":"D","text":"36"}],"answer":"D","topics":["counting"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":26},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-27","type":"mc","prompt":"How many whole numbers have squares that are between 2 and 200?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"13"},{"key":"C","text":"24"},{"key":"D","text":"26"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":27},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-28","type":"mc","prompt":"A baker cuts circular cookies out of a flat rectangle of cookie dough. If the rectangle is 2 m by 1 m, and the cookies have radius 10 cm, at most how many cookies can the baker cut from the sheet of dough?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"50"},{"key":"B","text":"63"},{"key":"C","text":"64"},{"key":"D","text":"200"}],"answer":"A","topics":["geometry","measurement"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":28},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-29","type":"mc","prompt":"0.02% of 20% of $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ = 200% of 2000","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1000"},{"key":"B","text":"100 000"},{"key":"C","text":"1 000 000"},{"key":"D","text":"100 000 000"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":29},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-30","type":"mc","prompt":"A miner combines 1200 kg of ore that is on average 3% gold with 2400 kg of ore that is on average 6% gold. If the 100 kg containing the most gold of the 3600 kg is 40% gold, the remaining ore will be $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ gold.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2%"},{"key":"B","text":"3%"},{"key":"C","text":"4%"},{"key":"D","text":"5%"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals","rates"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":30},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-31","type":"mc","prompt":"Including face diagonals, the total number of diagonals of a cube is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"14"},{"key":"C","text":"16"},{"key":"D","text":"24"}],"answer":"C","topics":["geometry","counting"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":31},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-32","type":"mc","prompt":"How many odd 3-digit integers greater than 500 are composed of 3 different non-zero digits?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"154"},{"key":"B","text":"175"},{"key":"C","text":"185"},{"key":"D","text":"200"}],"answer":"A","topics":["counting"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":32},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-33","type":"mc","prompt":"If I square all whole-number factors of 36 and multiply the resulting numbers, the product will be equal to","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$36^2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$36^4$"},{"key":"C","text":"$36^8$"},{"key":"D","text":"$36^9$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":33},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-34","type":"mc","prompt":"When the four members of the Beaverton family carry a log, each has a 0.02 probability of tripping, and each probability is independent of the others. What is the probability that they will carry the log without any of them tripping?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$1-(0.02)^4$"},{"key":"B","text":"$(0.98)^4$"},{"key":"C","text":"$(0.02)^4$"},{"key":"D","text":"$1-(0.98)^4$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["probability"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":34},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g8-35","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the largest prime factor of the product of all even numbers from 2 through 200?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"47"},{"key":"B","text":"97"},{"key":"C","text":"199"},{"key":"D","text":"2019"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":35}]}